ST1 License
===========

ST1 is an Atari ST decompression project for the ZX1 data compression format.
It contains the ST1 resumable 68000 decompressors, the supporting Java jx1 and
C# nx1 tools and reference implementations, and related experiments. It
follows the dual licensing structure of the original ZX1 (see c/zx1/LICENSE
and the License section of c/zx1/README.md):

1. THE COMPRESSOR - the Java and C# compressors and optimal parsers (Block,
   Optimizer, Compressor, Java Jx1, C# Nx1, and the retired compressor
   experiments), derived from Einar Saukas' optimal C compressor - is
   available under the BSD 3-Clause License below. In practice this is
   relevant only if you modify its source code and/or incorporate the
   compressor within your own products; if you just execute it to compress
   files, you can simply ignore these conditions.

2. THE DECOMPRESSORS - Java Decompressor/Djx1, C# Decompressor/Dnx1, the ST1
   decompressors in 68k/ (ST1.S, ST1_wrap.S, and ST1_ring.S), the YX6 chiptune
   player in yx6/ (YX6.S and YX6_player.S), and the retired decompressor
   variants in retired/68k/ (including jx1_68000_ring_mod.S) - can be used
   freely within your own programs (for any platform), even for commercial
   releases. The only condition is that you must indicate somehow in your
   documentation that you have used ZX1, via ST1, jx1, or nx1.

Attribution
-----------

* The ZX1 data compression format and algorithm was designed and implemented
  by Einar Saukas (Copyright (c) 2021), with thanks to introspec/spke. The
  original C and z80 sources are vendored unmodified under c/zx1/ with their
  own LICENSE.
* The additions and differences to the original (custom buffer/backreference
  sizes, the incremental ring buffer, resumable decompression, the ST1/68000
  target, and the direction of the optimization campaign - see README.md) are
  Copyright (c) 2026 Robbert van Dalen.
* The Java port, first ST1/68000 decompressor variants,
  emulation/measurement rigs, the YX6 chiptune packer and player, and retired
  optimization documentation were written by Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code).
  The C# nx1 port and the ST1_wrap.S counted-wrap decoder and tests were
  written by OpenAI Codex. Both were developed under the direction of Robbert
  van Dalen.
* The YM6 register-dump format is by Arnaud Carré (Leonard/Oxygene); YX6 reads
  it and is inspired by Steve Clarets' MinYMiser player.

